# Admin button and field sizing

## Height

- `.admin-input` and `.admin-btn` share `--admin-control-height` (44px) in `public/css/admin.css`.
- `.admin-btn--sm` is **not** shorter — it only reduces horizontal padding/font for compact toolbars.
- Only `.admin-btn--lg` may be taller (hero CTAs).

## Filter bars

- Use `.cp-filters` grid with **one `.cp-filter` per control** (label + field).
- Put Apply/Reset in a separate `.cp-filter.cp-filter--actions` column — never in the same flex row as a labeled select (stretch made buttons too tall).
- Grid variants: default 6-col (projects list with Show), `.cp-filters--5col`, `.cp-filters--3col`.

## Inline rows

- `.admin-list-filters` and `.cp-filters .cp-filter--actions` use `align-items: flex-end`.
- Buttons get `align-self: flex-end` and `flex-shrink: 0`.

## Do not

- Add page-specific `min-height` on buttons unless it equals `--admin-control-height`.
- Invent new button size classes; extend `admin-btn` modifiers in `admin.css` instead.

See `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` § Buttons.
